      { t: "mcq", q: "In paragraph 4, 'endeavour to keep their work voice separate' means that many workers …", o: ["try hard to", "refuse to", "are forced to", "forget to"], a: 0, x: "endeavour = يسعى جاهداً ويحاول بجدّ (try hard)." },
      { t: "mcq", q: "Why does the writer mention a funeral and a crucial interview in paragraph 5?", o: ["To prove that brave faces are always harmful", "To suggest that people should avoid such events", "To show that self-control can sometimes be positive", "To criticise people who attend funerals"], a: 2, x: "هذه أمثلة على لحظات يكون فيها ضبط النفس قوة ولطفاً (self-control is both a strength and a kindness)، فهي تدعم فكرة أن الوجه الشجاع قد يكون مفيداً أحياناً." },
      { t: "tf", q: "The writer claims that suppression is the only cause of headaches and poor sleep.", a: false, x: "الفقرة 2: الأطباء ينسبون الأعراض إلى mixture of causes rather than hidden feelings alone، والكاتب نفسه يستخدم عبارات تحوّط مثل may وcould." },
      { t: "find", q: "Find a word in paragraph 4 that means 'extremely tired and without energy'.", a: ["drained"], x: "drained = منهَك تماماً." },
      { t: "open", q: "Do you think it is better to put on a brave face or to show how you feel? Give one reason.", m: "I think it depends on the situation. In a job interview, a brave face is sensible, because it helps you stay calm and professional. With close friends, however, I would show how I feel, because talking honestly makes a problem feel lighter.", x: "تُقبل أي إجابة تعبّر عن رأي واضح مع سبب بجملة كاملة، ويُفضَّل استعمال عبارات التحوّط (it depends, may, tends to)." }
