    {
      id: "g12u10-gr3",
      title: "Pronouns before a gerund, and exam traps",
      ar: "الضمير قبل الـ gerund، وفخاخ الامتحان (to + gerund وغيرها)",
      body: [
        { p: "هذا الدرس يجمع نقطتين تتكرران في الامتحان: ماذا نضع **قبل الـ gerund** (صفة ملكية مثل my أم ضمير مفعولي مثل me؟)، ثم **فخاخ** يقع فيها حتى الطلاب الجيدون، وأهمها الكلمة **to** التي يأتي بعدها gerund." },
        { h: "1) الضمير قبل الـ gerund" },
        { p: "عندما يكون للـ gerund **فاعل خاص به** (أي من يقوم بالفعل) نضع قبله إما **صفة ملكية** (my, your, his, her, our, their أو 's)، أو **ضميراً مفعولياً** (me, you, him, her, us, them). الصيغتان صحيحتان، والفرق في **درجة الرسمية**:" },
        { table: { head: ["الأسلوب", "التركيب", "مثال"], rows: [
          ["رسمي (كتابة، رسائل، امتحانات)", "possessive + V-ing", "I appreciate ==your helping== me. / She was upset about ==Karim's leaving==."],
          ["عادي (كلام يومي)", "object pronoun / noun + V-ing", "I appreciate ==you helping== me. / She was upset about ==Karim leaving==."]
        ] } },
        { ex: [
          ["Do you mind ==my opening== the window?", "هل تمانع في أن أفتح النافذة؟ (رسمي)"],
          ["Do you mind ==me opening== the window?", "هل تمانع في أن أفتح النافذة؟ (عادي)"],
          ["We were grateful for ==their responding== so quickly.", "كنا ممتنين لأنهم ردّوا بهذه السرعة."],
          ["==His being== late annoyed everyone.", "تأخّره أزعج الجميع. (في بداية الجملة نفضّل الصفة الملكية)"]
        ] },
        { p: "**متى نستخدم الصيغة العادية (المفعولية) فقط؟** (أ) مع الكلمات التي ليس لها شكل ملكي مناسب: someone, everybody, nobody, this, those, both. (ب) مع العبارات الطويلة: I was surprised at the head of the department resigning. (ج) **بعد أفعال الإدراك** see, hear, watch, notice, feel: المقصود رؤية الشخص وهو يفعل الفعل، فنستخدم الضمير المفعولي ولا نستخدم الملكي." },
        { ex: [
          ["I can't imagine ==anybody refusing== such a generous offer.", "لا أتصوّر أن يرفض أحد عرضاً سخياً كهذا."],
          ["She was surprised at ==the manager resigning== so suddenly.", "فوجئت باستقالة المدير المفاجئة."],
          ["I saw ==him leaving== the building at midnight.", "رأيته يغادر المبنى عند منتصف الليل."]
        ] },
        { warn: "✗ I saw his leaving the building. ← ✓ I saw ==him leaving== the building. (مع see / hear / watch نستخدم الضمير المفعولي)" },
        { h: "2) الفخ الأكبر: to حرف جر وليست علامة المصدر" },
        { p: "كلمة **to** ليست دائماً علامة المصدر. في تعابير كثيرة تكون **حرف جر** (preposition)، وبعد حرف الجر نستخدم V-ing أو اسماً. **اختبار سريع:** إذا استطعتَ أن تضع بعد to كلمة it أو اسماً (to it / to the idea) فإن to حرف جر ويأتي بعدها V-ing؛ فنقول I look forward to ==it== ثم I look forward to ==meeting== you. أما I want to it فغير ممكنة، لأن want to هنا علامة المصدر." },
        { table: { head: ["التعبير", "المعنى", "مثال"], rows: [
          ["look forward to", "يتطلّع إلى", "I look forward to ==hearing== from you."],
          ["object to", "يعترض على", "Many staff object to ==working== at weekends."],
          ["be committed / dedicated / devoted to", "ملتزم بـ / مكرّس لـ", "The firm is committed to ==protecting== the environment."],
          ["be used to / get used to", "معتاد على / يعتاد على", "I'm not used to ==getting== up so early."],
          ["in addition to", "بالإضافة إلى", "In addition to ==teaching==, she writes textbooks."],
          ["with a view to", "بهدف", "He took evening classes with a view to ==changing== careers."],
          ["when it comes to", "عندما يتعلق الأمر بـ", "When it comes to ==making== decisions, she is very quick."],
          ["prefer X to Y", "يفضّل X على Y", "I prefer ==working== in a team to ==working== alone."],
          ["lead to / contribute to / resort to", "يؤدي إلى / يساهم في / يلجأ إلى", "Long hours can lead to ==feeling== exhausted."],
          ["admit to / confess to", "يعترف بـ", "He admitted to ==taking== the money."]
        ] } },
        { tip: "قارن: **used to + V1** = كنتُ أفعل في الماضي (I ==used to live== in Irbid)، و**be used to + V-ing** = معتاد على (I'm ==used to living== alone)، و**get used to + V-ing** = أتعوّد على (I'm ==getting used to living== alone)." },
        { warn: "✗ I look forward to hear from you. ← ✓ I look forward to ==hearing== from you. ✗ We are committed to provide quality. ← ✓ We are committed to ==providing== quality. ✗ I'm used to get up early. ← ✓ I'm used to ==getting== up early." },
        { h: "3) تعبيرات يأتي بعدها V-ing مباشرة" },
        { table: { head: ["التعبير", "مثال"], rows: [
          ["It's no use / It's no good + V-ing", "It's no use ==complaining==; nobody will listen."],
          ["It's (not) worth + V-ing", "The museum is well worth ==visiting==."],
          ["There's no point in + V-ing", "There's no point in ==waiting== any longer."],
          ["What's the point of / the use of + V-ing", "What's the point of ==studying== if you don't understand?"],
          ["It's a waste of time / money + V-ing", "It's a waste of time ==worrying== about it."],
          ["have difficulty / trouble (in) + V-ing", "She had trouble ==finding== a job."],
          ["spend / waste time + V-ing; be busy + V-ing", "He spends hours ==answering== emails."],
          ["can't stand / feel like + V-ing", "I can't stand ==waiting== in queues."]
        ] } },
        { warn: "✗ There's no point of arguing. / ✗ There's no point to argue. ← ✓ There's no point ==in arguing==. (حرف الجر الصحيح هو in)" },
        { warn: "✗ The film is worth to see. / ✗ The film is worth seeing it. ← ✓ The film is worth ==seeing==. (بعد worth نستخدم V-ing، ولا نكرر المفعول it)" },
        { tip: "هذه التعبيرات تأتي في أسئلة إعادة الصياغة بصيغة: It's pointless to argue. = There's no point in ==arguing==. / It's useless to complain. = It's no use ==complaining==. احفظها كوحدات كاملة." }
      ],
      summary: [
        "قبل الـ gerund: صفة ملكية (my, your, his…) في الأسلوب الرسمي، أو ضمير مفعولي (me, him…) في الأسلوب العادي. وبعد see / hear / watch نستخدم المفعولي فقط.",
        "to حرف جر (فيأتي بعدها V-ing) في: look forward to, object to, be committed / dedicated / devoted to, be / get used to, in addition to, with a view to, prefer X to Y.",
        "اختبار it: إذا صحّ أن تضع it بعد to فهي حرف جر ← V-ing (I look forward to it ← to meeting).",
        "It's no use / no good + V-ing؛ It's worth + V-ing (بلا مفعول مكرر)؛ There's no point in + V-ing؛ It's a waste of time + V-ing.",
        "have difficulty / trouble + V-ing؛ spend / waste time + V-ing؛ be busy + V-ing؛ can't stand + V-ing."
      ],
      qs: [
        { t: "mcq", q: "I really appreciate ____ me with the report.", o: ["you to help", "your helping", "you help", "yours helping"], a: 1, x: "بعد appreciate نستخدم gerund، وقبله صفة ملكية في الأسلوب الرسمي ← your helping. أما you to help وyou help فتركيب خاطئ، وyours ضمير مستقل لا يأتي قبل الـ gerund." },
        { t: "mcq", q: "The union strongly objects ____ longer working hours.", o: ["to introducing", "introducing", "to introduce", "for introducing"], a: 0, x: "object to: كلمة to هنا حرف جر، فيأتي بعدها gerund ← objects to introducing." },
        { t: "gap", q: "It's no good ____ (wait) any longer; the shop closed an hour ago.", a: ["waiting"], x: "It's no good + V-ing ← waiting." },
        { t: "mcq", q: "I'm looking forward ____ you at the conference.", o: ["to see", "seeing", "to seeing", "for seeing"], a: 2, x: "look forward to + V-ing؛ فـ to هنا حرف جر (اختبار it: I look forward to it) ← looking forward to seeing." },
        { t: "gap", q: "She devoted her life to ____ (help) refugee children.", a: ["helping"], x: "devote yourself to: كلمة to حرف جر فيأتي بعدها gerund ← devoted her life to helping." },
        { t: "mcq", q: "It's no use ____ with him; he never changes his mind.", o: ["to argue", "argue", "of arguing", "arguing"], a: 3, x: "It's no use + V-ing ← arguing. لا نستخدم to-infinitive ولا حرف جر بعد no use." },
        { t: "mcq", q: "Do you mind ____ the window? It's very hot in here.", o: ["I opening", "me to open", "mine opening", "my opening"], a: 3, x: "Do you mind + صفة ملكية (أو ضمير مفعولي me) + V-ing ← my opening. لا نضع ضمير الفاعل I قبل الـ gerund." },
        { t: "gap", q: "Do you mind ____ (I / borrow: use -ing) your pen for a minute?", a: ["my borrowing", "me borrowing"], x: "قبل الـ gerund نضع صفة ملكية (my borrowing) في الأسلوب الرسمي أو ضميراً مفعولياً (me borrowing) في الأسلوب العادي. (أما Do you mind if I borrow…? فتركيب صحيح وشائع أيضاً، لكن المطلوب هنا gerund مع ضمير قبله.)" },
        { t: "mcq", q: "The company is fully committed ____ equal opportunities for all.", o: ["to provide", "to providing", "providing", "in providing"], a: 1, x: "be committed to + V-ing؛ كلمة to هنا حرف جر ← committed to providing." },
        { t: "gap", q: "I strongly object ____ (treat) like a child.", a: ["to being treated", "to my being treated"], x: "object to حرف جر فنحتاج gerund، ولأن المتحدث هو من يُعامَل ← مبني للمجهول: to being treated." },
        { t: "mcq", q: "That film is well worth ____.", o: ["to watch", "watching it", "watching", "to be watching"], a: 2, x: "worth + V-ing ← worth watching. لا نستخدم to-infinitive بعد worth ولا نكرر المفعول it." },
        { t: "mcq", q: "I saw ____ leaving the building at midnight.", o: ["his", "he", "him", "he's"], a: 2, x: "بعد see / hear / watch نستخدم ضميراً مفعولياً + V-ing ← him leaving. لا نستخدم الصفة الملكية ولا ضمير الفاعل." },
        { t: "gap", q: "She prefers working in a team ____ (work) alone.", a: ["to working", "rather than working"], x: "prefer X to Y: كلمة to حرف جر، فيأتي بعدها gerund ← prefers working in a team to working alone. (ويُقبل أيضاً rather than working.)" },
        { t: "tr", q: "It is pointless to argue with her.", p: "Rewrite starting with: There's no point …", a: ["There's no point in arguing with her.", "There is no point in arguing with her.", "There's no point arguing with her.", "There is no point arguing with her."], x: "There's no point in + V-ing ← in arguing. (ويجوز حذف in في الكلام العادي: There's no point arguing.)" },
        { t: "tr", q: "I hope to hear from you soon.", p: "Rewrite starting with: I look forward …", a: ["I look forward to hearing from you soon."], x: "look forward to + V-ing؛ to هنا حرف جر ← to hearing." },
        { t: "err", q: "There's no point of arguing with him.", w: "of", c: "in", x: "التعبير الصحيح: There's no point in + V-ing." },
        { t: "err", q: "I'm not used to work under so much pressure.", w: "work", c: "working", x: "be used to + V-ing؛ فـ to هنا حرف جر ← I'm not used to working." },
        { t: "order", a: "The old city is well worth exploring.", x: "worth + V-ing: is well worth exploring." }
      ]
    }
